4. Receive live attenuated vaccine or vaccine within 4 weeks prior to the first study drug treatment or plan to receive live vaccine during the study period;
5. Subjects with active or pre-existing autoimmune diseases that are likely to recur, or patients at high risk (such as those who have received an organ transplant and require immunosuppressive therapy).

Inclusion Criteria:

1. Aged 18 years old or above;
2. Patients with previous pathological diagnosis of 2021 World Health Organization Classification of Central Nervous System Tumors (WHO CNS5) grade 3 or 4 glioma and received standard treatment;
